      {
        "@value": "The traditional cigar package, widely credited to H. Upmann in the early 1800s; US law since 1865 requires wooden boxes in counts of 25, 50, 100, or 250; Spanish cedar is the most common material."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
